Package: secubox-meshtastic
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
 python3 (>= 3.11),
 python3-fastapi,
 python3-uvicorn,
 python3-pydantic,
 python3-paho-mqtt,
 secubox-core,
 sudo
Recommends: mosquitto, python3-segno
Description: SecuBox-Deb Meshtastic LoRa node integration
 Native Python module for managing Meshtastic LoRa mesh nodes: radio/cache/
 passive-listener/MQTT-bridge daemon (secubox-meshtasticd), privileged CLI
 (secubox-meshtasticctl) and webui panel (/meshtastic/, own dedicated
 socket — never served by the aggregator).
 .
 The upstream `meshtastic` Python library (device/BLE/serial protocol) is
 NOT packaged for Debian and is intentionally NOT a dependency here: the
 daemon runs fine with `radio: absent` (cache/passive/bridge only) without
 it, and it is only required once a physical Meshtastic device is attached.
 See README.md for the pip/venv install note.
